@page "/components/sheet"

<PageTitle>Sheet — Unpoly.Blazor.Shadcn</PageTitle>

<h1 class="doc-h1">Sheet</h1>
<p class="doc-lede">
    A panel from an edge. Structurally identical to <a href="/components/dialog">Dialog</a> — a
    native <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code> with the shadcn panel inside — and the only difference is
    which edge it is pinned to.
</p>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Basic</h2>
<Example Source="SheetExample.razor"><SheetExample /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">Side</h2>
<Example Source="SheetSide.razor"><SheetSide /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">No Close Button</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    Escape and the backdrop still close it — both belong to the <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code>, not to
    the button. But a panel with no visible way out is one people learn to distrust, so leave it
    off only when the footer carries one.
</p>
<Example Source="SheetNoClose.razor"><SheetNoClose /></Example>

<h2 class="doc-h2">RTL</h2>
<p class="doc-note">
    <code>Side="right"</code> still means the right of the screen: a drawer is a physical place,
    not a reading edge. What mirrors is the content inside it.
</p>
<Example Source="SheetRtl.razor"><SheetRtl /></Example>
